    <title>New generation Chameleons &amp; LEA Products</title>
    <author>
      <name>Lab401 Steve</name>
    </author>
    <summary type="html">
      <![CDATA[New generation Chameleon products are in stock; Pentester packs have been updated; Law Enforcement and Enterprise Tools have been created - and we even made some great stickers.<p><a class="read-more" href="https://lab401.com/blogs/news/new-generation-chameleons-lea-products">More</a></p>]]>
    </summary>
    <content type="html">
      <![CDATA[<h2>Lab401 in 2020</h2>
<p><strong>It's been a busy start to the year at Lab401.</strong> The new generation Chameleon products are in stock; all our pentester packs have been updated to the latest generation tools, and we've also launched the Law Enforcement and Enterprise tools.</p>
<h2>LEA Products</h2>
<p>In order to support the needs to the Law Enforcement and Government Services, Lab401 has opened its <a href="https://lab401.com/collections/lea-tools"><strong>LEA Tools</strong></a> section.</p>
<p>We have high performance tools for demanding situations - RF, RFID and Automotive solutions.</p>
<p>Access to LEA products is restricted to verified Law Enforcement bodies, Government Services and their suppliers. For access, <strong><a href="mailto:support@lab401.com">please contact customer support</a></strong> from an official email account, or with your credentials, and we will grant access.</p>
<p>We have also opened our <a href="https://lab401.com/collections/enterprise-tools"><strong>Enterprise Tools</strong></a> section, with tools restricted to verifiable enterprise clients in the pentesting industry. Our tools are exclusive to Lab401, highly specialised, and already used in the field and lab for special operations.</p>
<p>As with the LEA Tools, <a href="mailto:support@lab401.com"><strong>please send an email to Lab401 support</strong></a> to get access to the Enterprise Tools.</p>
<h2>Brand New Chameleons</h2>
<p>The new generation of Chameleon devices are finally available. The Proxgrind Chameleon devices are the latest evolution of the KAOS RevG devices.</p>
<p>There are two flavours of device: the RevG and the ChameleonTiny.</p>
<p><img src="//cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/2175/8571/files/ChameleonMini-vs-ChameleonTiny_large.png?v=1581684932" alt=""></p>
<h3>Product Comparison</h3>
<p>There are several ChameleonMini devices available. The table below breaks down the differences in detail.</p>
<p>If your are a <strong>penetration tester </strong>/ researcher, or require wireless functionality, Lab401 recommends the <strong>ChameleonMini RevG by Proxgrind.</strong></p>
<p>If <strong></strong>you are looking to store all your tags in one device, or size is the most important factor for you, Lab401 recommends the <a href="https://lab401.com/products/chameleontiny"><strong>ChameleonTiny.</strong></a></p>
